   "evidence": "mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Ideal/Operations.lean:382 `instance (priority := low) : (I ^ n).IsTwoSided` (under `variable [I.IsTwoSided]`, line 380); :375 `instance [J.IsTwoSided] : (I * J).IsTwoSided`; :354 `theorem pow_le_pow_right {m n : \u2115} (h : m \u2264 n) : I ^ n \u2264 I ^ m`; :272 `theorem one_eq_top : (1 : Ideal R) = \u22a4`; mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Ideal/Defs.lean:64 `theorem mul_mem_right (b : \u03b1) (I : Ideal \u03b1) [I.IsTwoSided]`. The PR's `I` already carries `[I.IsTwoSided]` (GolodShafarevich.lean:70).",
   "file": "TauCeti/RingTheory/Ideal/GolodShafarevich.lean",
   "fix": "Set `P : \u2115 \u2192 Submodule k A := fun m \u21a6 (I ^ m).restrictScalars k`. Then `hP0` is `Ideal.one_eq_top`, `hPsucc` is `Submodule.pow_succ`, `hright` becomes `Ideal.mul_mem_right` (via the `(I ^ m).IsTwoSided` instance), `hanti` becomes `Ideal.pow_le_pow_right`, and `hc1` follows from `hI` directly since `P 1 = I.restrictScalars k`. `hmem` and `hsurj` go through unchanged (`Ideal.mul_mem_mul`, `Submodule.mul_induction_on'`).",
   "issue": "`P m := \u22a4 * J ^ m` with `J = I.restrictScalars k` obscures that the filtration is just `I ^ m`, and forces the 8-line nested induction `hright` (lines 83-90) re-proving that `P m` is a right ideal, plus the ad hoc `hle : P 1 \u2264 J` inside `hc1` (line 115). Mathlib already has `Ideal.IsTwoSided` instances giving `(I ^ m).IsTwoSided` from `[I.IsTwoSided]`, so these are hand-rolled reproofs of existing API inside an already 53-line proof.",
   "line": 76
  }
 ],
